course: dictionary
lesson: 14058
title: Words for helpers
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A masseur is a person whose job is to give massages. A massage means rubbing and pressing the muscles to help them relax or heal. «After the football match, the masseur rubbed the sore muscles in Sam's legs.» The clues are football match and sore muscles, so a masseur helps tired or hurt muscles.
explain: Use the context to check your meaning. Look at what the masseur does in the sentence: rubs and presses. Swap in your meaning: "the person whose job is to rub and press muscles" still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Some words are only used for men or women in older books. «Masseur» was used for a man, and a woman who did the job was called a masseuse. Today many people say «massage therapist» instead, which can be used for anyone.
fact: A masseur is a person whose job is to give massages.
fact: A massage means rubbing and pressing the muscles to help them relax or heal.
fact: Sports teams often have a masseur to help players with sore muscles.
fact: «Masseur» is an old-use word for a man; a woman was called a masseuse.
fact: Today many people say «massage therapist» instead.
exercise: «The runner had sore legs, so she went to see the masseur.» What is a masseur? | A doctor who gives injections | *A person whose job is to give massages | A teacher of sport | A person who runs races
exercise: What does a masseur do? | Cooks meals for the team | Sells sports kit | Takes photos of the players | *Rubs and presses muscles to help them relax
exercise: Which word could you use today instead of masseur? | Gardener | Cook | Referee | *Massage therapist
test: «After the match, the masseur helped the player's sore calf muscles.» Why did the player need the masseur? | To find his lost boots | To judge the game | To cook his tea | *To ease his sore muscles
test: Which is the old word for a woman who gives massages? | Mass | Masseur | *Masseuse | Massager
exam: Which sentence uses masseur correctly? | I took my dog to the masseur for its walk | The masseur swam across the lake | Masseur is a colour | *I booked an appointment with a masseur to help my aching back
